The attached image (Figure 4 from the PDF) illustrates the uptake of Nano-11 nanoparticles and ovalbumin (OVA) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) using confocal microscopy. It demonstrates that while soluble OVA (green) shows modest uptake, Nano-11 (red) is efficiently internalized by BMDCs. Critically, when BMDCs are incubated with Nano-11 adsorbed OVA, both components are taken up in large amounts and extensively co-localize within the cells, confirming that Nano-11 significantly enhances the intracellular delivery of antigens to dendritic cells and maintains association with the antigen after uptake.